  "text": "Elections and Results | Guilford County\nSkip to main content\nAn official website of the State of North Carolina\nAn official website of NC\nHow you know\nState Government websites value user privacy. To learn more,\nview our full privacy policy\n.\nSecure websites use HTTPS certificates. A lock icon or https:// means you\u2019ve safely connected to the official website.\nUtility Menu\nNews\nJobs\nCounty Directory\nEmergency Notifications\nPublic Records Request\nMain menu\nI Want To\nI Want To\nApply for a Building Permit\nAdopt a Pet\nAccess the GIS Online Services\nApply for a Marriage License\nGet a Birth or Death Certificate\nRegister to Vote\nView Arrest Records\nView and Pay Taxes\nLiving\nWorking\nMy Property\nGovernment\nGovernment\nBoard of Commissioners\nBoard of Elections\nCounty Attorney's Office\nCounty Manager\nCountywide Programs and Initiatives\nDepartments and Agencies\nRegister of Deeds\nSheriff's Office\nUtility Menu\nNews\nJobs\nCounty Directory\nEmergency Notifications\nPublic Records Request\nSearch\nHome\nGovernment\nBoard of Elections\nElections and Results\nSVG\nMarch 3, 2026 Primary Reports\nView the official results of the March 3, 2026 Primary Election certified by the Guilford County Board of Elections at Canvass on Friday, March 13. Results are compiled by the County and have been updated to include results of recounts. These results will be updated to include full precinct totals once the precinct sort is complete.\nElection Results Dashboard\nLinks directly to the NCSBE Elections Results Dashboard to view Guilford County and all election results. On election day, this dashboard provides live results after polls close at 7:30 p.m. County election results have been certified by the local Board of Elections at Canvass.\nThe two links below will also access the North Carolina State Board of Elections website and election results information.\nGuilford County Results\n, all contests\nNorth Carolina\n, all contests\n(select applicable Criteria to see any North Carolina county or statewide results; see FAQ below for more information)\nThe dashboard may also be used to access previous election results.\nHow to Use the Election Results Dashboard and Frequently Asked Questions\nWhat is the Election Results Dashboard?\nWhen is the Dashboard Updated on Election Night?\nHow Do I Use the Dashboard?\nHow do I Explore More Election Results?\nWhat is the Election Results Dashboard?\nThe Election Results Dashboard displays live election results and is updated every 10 minutes. The dashboard goes live after polls close. The Dashboard also allows you to:\nExplore data via breakout maps, tables, and charts.\nDownload election results data spreadsheets.\nAccess historical election results.\nWhen is the Dashboard Updated on Election Night?\nOnce polls close on election night, the dashboard is updated every 10 minutes as precincts report results to the North Carolina State Board of Elections.\nHow Do I Use the Dashboard?\nTo view election results, follow these steps:\nGo to the dashboard through one of the above links.\nTo change information that auto-populates, select the desired election date, county (or choose \"state\" for statewide results), office, and contest.\nClick \"Display Results\".\nClick \"Refresh\" often to view the most recent results.\nHow do I Explore More Election Results?\nPerform the steps listed under \"How Do I Use the Dashboard?\".\nClick \"View Contest Details\".\nThe \"Contest Details\" tab provides the total number of votes received by each candidate or ballot item, along with a map showing the winner of each county.\nThe \"Results by Voting Method\" tab provides a table with a breakdown of votes cast by method (e.g., in-person on Election Day, absentee by-mail, etc.).\nThe \"Results by Contest\" tab provides a table with a breakdown of votes cast in each county.\nClick \"Refresh\" often to view the most recent results.\nElection results are unofficial until certified through the Canvass process; certified results are posted after Canvass. The reports posted below will designate if the results are unofficial or certified. Contact our office at 336-641-3836 if any questions on election results or email us at\nguilfordelections@guilfordcountync.gov\nwith a specific data request.\nPast Elections Results Archive\nPrimary Elections\nGeneral Elections\nPrimary Elections\nMarch 3, 2026\nOctober 7, 2025\nMay 14, 2024\nMarch 5, 2024\nOctober 10, 2023\nMay 17, 2022\nOctober 5, 2021\nMarch 3, 2020\nOctober 8, 2019\nMay 8, 2018\nOctober 10, 2017\nMarch 15, 2016\nJune 7, 2016\nOctober 6, 2015\nJuly 15, 2014\nGeneral Elections\nNovember 4, 2025\nNovember 5, 2024\nNovember 07, 2023\nNovember 08, 2022\nJuly 26, 2022\nNovember 02, 2021\nNovember 03, 2020\nNovember 05, 2019\nNovember 06, 2018\nNovember 07, 2017\nNovember 08, 2016\nNovember 03, 2015\nNovember 04, 2014\nOn This Page Jump Links\nOff\nSide Nav\nBoard of Elections\nAbsentee Voting Information\nCalendar Dates and Deadlines\nCampaign Finance\nCandidate Filing Information\nContact Board of Elections\nElections and Results\nGuilford County Board of Elections Meetings\nVoting Information\nElection Day Voting\nEarly Voting\nGuilford County\nContact Us\nGuilford County Government\n301 W. Market St.\nGreensboro, NC 27401\nMonday through Friday, 8 a.m. to 5 p.m.\nContact Us\nFollow Us\nStay Connected\nSign Up for County News\nNetwork Menu\nnc.gov\nWebsite Feedback\nAccessibility\nDisclaimer & Terms of Use\nPrivacy Policy\nOpen Budget\nHosted on Digital Commons",
